timestamp=2026-11-04T16:04:59.918Z level=INFO run=e9a56b16 message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python3 << 'PY'\nexec(open('/tmp/process_full.py').read())\nimport csv\nimport math\nfrom datetime import datetime\n\nrows = []\nwith open('/app/dataset/data.csv') as f:\n    reader = csv.DictReader(f)\n    for idx, row in enumerate(reader):\n        rid = row['record_id']\n        et = parse_event_time(row['event_time'])\n        region = row['region']\n        channel = row['channel']\n        amount = parse_amount(row['amount_str'])\n        notes = parse_notes(row['notes'])\n        if math.isnan(amount):\n            net = float('nan')\n        else:\n            if notes['waive']:\n                net = 0.0\n            else:\n                net = amount * (1.0 + notes['adj_pct']) + notes['fee']\n        rows.append({\n            'rid': rid,\n            'et': et,\n            'region': region,\n            'channel': channel,\n            'net': net,\n            'notes': notes,\n            'file_order': idx,\n        })\n\n# Deduplication: keep one row per record_id by choosing the latest event_time,\n# breaking ties by preferring the version with a real net result, then earlier file order.\n# Also \"keep only rows with non-missing event_time\" - but wait, the dedup happens before or after filtering?\n# The task says: \"after working out net, keep one row per record_id by choosing the latest event_time,\n# breaking ties by preferring the version with a real net result, then earlier file order.\n# Keep only rows with non-missing event_time, event_time between 2025-10-01 00:00:00 and 2025-12-31 23:59:59 inclusive,\n# channel != \\\"phone\\\" (case-insensitive), and finite net, ...\"\n# So deduplication is done AFTER working out net, but BEFORE or AFTER the filtering step that removes missing event_time? The ordering in the sentence: dedup first (choose latest etc), then \"Keep only rows...\" - those are subsequent filters applied. So we deduplicate all records to get one row per record_id, then apply the filters.\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
