timestamp=2026-11-04T16:09:14.892Z level=INFO run=e9a56b16 message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python3 << 'PY'\n# 77.860 with 3 digits after dot -> dot treated as not decimal by rule, removed -> 77860. That gives amount 77860.0. net = 77860.0 * (1 - 0.0521) + 4.9 = 77860.0 * 0.9479 + 4.9. 77860.0 * 0.9479: 77860.0 * (1 - 0.0521) = 77860.0 - 77860.0*0.0521 = 77860.0 - (77860.0*(52.1/1000)) roughly? 77860.0*0.0521: 77860.0*(0.05 + 0.0021) = 77860.0*0.05 + 77860.0*0.0021 = 3893.0 + 163.506 = 4056.506. So 77860.0 - 4056.506 = 73803.494. Plus 4.9 = 73808.394. Correct, matches.\n# So the amount parsing with the \"last separator, check digits after\" rule as written produces these large numbers. That’s what the rules say. We must follow them exactly.\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
