timestamp=2026-11-04T16:12:55.933Z level=INFO run=e9a56b16 message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python3 << 'PY'\n# Let us quickly sanity check a couple more edge cases we might have missed\n# For example, when items is missing -> items_eff should be 1. Also when items is 0 -> items becomes 0, then clamped to at least 1, so items_eff becomes 1 (log1p(1)=ln(2)~=0.693). Also if items is negative? The spec says items from items=<int> (missing -> None). We parse as int of the captured group - could be negative? We used (-?\\d+), so could get negative. But then \"items_eff as items if present else 1 (clamped to at least 1)\". So if items is present (not None) and is -5, then items_eff becomes max(-5, 1)? -5 clamped to at least 1 gives 1. That matches \"clamped to at least 1\". So our logic is correct.\n# Another check: waive is case-insensitive - we already handle (TRUE/true/tRue all match). Correct.\n# Channel comparison is case-insensitive and we exclude channel == \"phone\" - we do channel.strip().lower() == 'phone' -> so \"PHONE\", \" phone \", \"Phone\" all excluded. Correct.\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
